      "prompt": "Use the Skill to improve the link from an Introduction closing paragraph to a Methodology opening and a Conclusion for this fictional soft-sensor paper. Return those three paragraphs in English, then a brief revision note. The engineering task is predicting a continuous concentration from irregularly timestamped measurements and infrequent laboratory targets. The verified prior comparison uses fixed-index positions, discarding elapsed intervals. The new mechanism encodes elapsed observation intervals in the attention scores. Training combines a supervised concentration loss on labeled windows with reconstruction of deliberately masked observed measurements from both labeled and unlabeled training windows. Mask reconstruction is supporting machinery, not a separate novelty claim. Prediction uses only the encoder and regression head; no target or reconstruction decoder is present. Missing observations at acquisition are distinct from deliberate training masks. The train/test split and label availability are already verified; all observations used for a prediction are available by the decision time. The model improves held-out concentration MAE relative to the stated fixed-index baseline under the same inputs and training information. No experiments varying assay delay or transferring to a new site were conducted. The accepted Methods sentence 'The regression head maps the interval-aware representation to a concentration estimate.' is correct and should be kept. Avoid three disconnected lists of the same modules, but do not invent an online imputer or causal discovery objective. Do not invent numerical results, references or a second case study.",
